KNOWNBUG broken-smt-backend
x_literal_widening1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.in == 0 \|\| main\.r == main\.r: PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^Invariant check failed
--
Assigning a sized x literal (1'bx) to a wider variable aborts ebmc with
an invariant violation in the flattening back-end:

  File: flattening/boolbv_typecast.cpp:432 function: type_conversion
  Condition: src_width >= dest_width
  Reason: cannot extend bv-typed bitvector

The x literal has type bv[1], and the typecast to unsignedbv[32] that
the front-end emits for the assignment is a widening of a bv-typed
operand, which boolbvt::type_conversion refuses. The widening should be
done by the Verilog lowering (padding with x, 1800-2017 11.8.3) rather
than being left to the solver. An unsized 'bx does not trigger the
problem. The SMT2 back-end (--z3) handles the widening, so the test
is excluded from the SMT runs. Found in picorv32.v (decoded_imm <=
1'bx in the default branch of the immediate decoder).
